Focus on creating a complete, polished, production-ready FRONTEND ERP interface.
One important change I strongly recommend daa

Your actual business has a special requirement: one employee can do multiple works on the same day.

For example:

Kumar → Cleaning → Dyeing → Drying → Machine → Finishing

So don't make the employee table like:

Employee → Designation → One Salary

Instead use:

Employee → Work Entries → Rate → Quantity → Earnings

That will make your salary automation much more accurate.

And because your rates are approximate, the ERP should have a Wage Rate Master where you can change ₹5 to ₹6, ₹25 to ₹30, etc., without changing the software code.

The most important database/business relationship will eventually be:

Raw Material Batch → Production Batch → Employee Work → Wage → Finished Mat → Warehouse → Sales → Profit/Loss

That structure will let you calculate the actual cost of producing each mat, rather than only calculating total monthly expenses.



